package domain

// The core's messages (milestone 69, D-084). A message is `{code, id, params,
// message}`: `code` the error category, `id` a stable dotted name, `params` its values
// as strings, in the order its text names them, and `message` the English sentence.
// Every id and its English text live here; a call site names the id and passes the
// params (`core_msg`), so the text the CLI prints stays what it was.
//
// cfire errors carry only text, so an id never travels inside the error: a driver
// that shows a message (`--json`, an event to the page) finds its id again by
// matching the text against these templates (`core_message_of`), and the page does
// the same for an RPC that failed, from the templates `app_info` sends it.
//
// Principle 21: the core is never translated; the page renders `core.<id>` from its
// catalog and falls back to `message`. A param carries only what the English text
// already shows, never a secret (Principle 6).

pub type MessageDef struct {
    id:   str `json:"id"`
    code: str `json:"code"`
    text: str `json:"text"`
}

pub type CoreMessage struct {
    code:    str
    id:      str
    params:  []str
    message: str
}

